# Component spec YAML conventions

Spec files in `docs/_spec/components/` are the structured source of truth for each component. The `ds-component-doc` skill consumes these to generate Markdown pages.

## Required top-level fields

Every spec YAML must include these fields (use `TBD` for unknown values, never omit):

```
name            # PascalCase component name (e.g., Alert, StatusBar)
status          # Only "draft" or "ready"
figma           # Object: file, page, component_set, optional component_set_node_id
summary         # Object: purpose, when_to_use, when_not_to_use
anatomy         # Array of { id, description }
properties      # Array of { name, type, values, default, required, description }
content_guidelines  # Object: rules (array)
best_practices  # Object: do (array), dont (array)
accessibility   # Object: role, focus, hit_area, labeling
token_mapping   # Object: keyed by "{part}.{attribute}"
qa              # Array of verification statements
```

## Optional top-level fields

```
version               # Optional object: { spec, component } with SemVer values
related_components    # Optional array of snake_case component names (e.g., [button, tag])
```

## Field conventions

### `name`

- PascalCase, matching the Figma component set name exactly.

### `status`

- `draft`: Incomplete or unverified. `ready`: Reviewed and matches Figma.
- No other values allowed. `needs-review` is **not valid** here.

> **Note:** The `status` field in spec YAML is intentionally more restrictive than the `doc_status`
> field in markdown frontmatter. Markdown pages support a third state (`needs-review`) to signal
> that an already-published page needs re-validation after upstream changes. Spec files do not have
> this intermediate state — a spec is either incomplete (`draft`) or verified (`ready`).

### `figma`

- `file`: Figma file key (not full URL).
- `page`: Page name in Figma.
- `component_set`: Component set name (not node ID).
- `component_set_node_id`: Figma node id for deterministic placement (`123:456` format).
  - Recommended in `draft`.
  - Required in `ready`.
  - If provided, skills that need deterministic Figma lookup must use this value.

### `anatomy`

- Each item has `id` (snake_case, e.g., `leading_icon`) and `description`.
- Order matches visual top-to-bottom / left-to-right reading order.

### `properties`

- Must map 1:1 with the Figma component set properties.
- `type`: Use canonical spec types - `enum`, `text`, `boolean`, `instance_swap`.
- `values`: Array of allowed values for `enum`; omit for `text`, `boolean`, and `instance_swap`.
- `default`: The Figma default value.
- `required`: `true` or `false`.
- Ordering MUST be deterministic and follow `component-spec-properties-order.mdc`.

**Type mapping decision table** - canonical source of truth. All other rules and skills must reference this table, not duplicate it.

Type comparison is **case-insensitive** (`Enum`, `ENUM`, and `enum` are equivalent).

| Spec `type` | Figma display type | `values` field | `default` format | Ordering group | On unknown |
| ----------- | ------------------ | -------------- | ---------------- | -------------- | ---------- |
| `enum` | `VARIANT` | Required - array of allowed string values | One of the `values` entries, or `TBD` if unknown | 1 | - |
| `text` | `TEXT` | Omit | Any string, or `TBD` if unknown | 2 | - |
| `boolean` | `BOOLEAN` | Omit | `true` or `false` (unquoted), or `TBD` if unknown | 3 | - |
| `instance_swap` | `INSTANCE_SWAP` | Omit | Component name string, or `TBD` if unknown | 4 | - |
| anything else (including `null`, `""`, missing) | _(invalid)_ | - | - | 5 | Stop; report error `SPEC01` with the invalid type value; do not render the property |

The "Stop; report error" instruction applies to **generating skills and scripts** (for example `ds:component-doc`, `ds:spec-from-figma`) and to `validate:docs`. Specs that violate this table are invalid and must be fixed before markdown generation.

Ready spec constraint:

- For `status: ready`, all property defaults must be concrete (not `TBD`), and `enum` defaults must match one of the `values`.

### `best_practices`

- Always include both `do` and `dont` arrays.
- Minimum 1 item each, or a single `TBD` entry.
- Items are short imperative sentences.

### `accessibility`

- `role`: ARIA role (e.g., `alert`, `button`, `navigation`). Use `TBD` if unknown.
- `focus.tokens`: Must reference real token paths for inner/outer focus outlines.
- `hit_area`: Must reference A11y collection tokens for desktop and mobile.
- `labeling.rules`: Array of labeling guidelines.

### `token_mapping`

- Keys follow pattern: `{anatomy_id}.{css_property}` (e.g., `container.background`, `label.color`).
- Values are objects keyed by condition (e.g., `"state=default"`, `"type=warning"`).
- Token paths must be real JSON keys - follow `prohibited-patterns.mdc`.
- Use `TBD` as value when token is unknown.

### `related_components` (optional)

- Array of `snake_case` component slugs (no file extensions).
- Duplicates are not allowed (case-insensitive).
- Must not include the current component's slug.
- For `status: ready`, every entry must resolve to an existing spec file at `docs/_spec/components/<slug>.yml`.

## Deterministic placement contract

- `figma.component_set_node_id` is the canonical traceability key for render placement.
- Resolution precedence in runtime tools should be:
  1. explicit CLI override (for controlled/manual execution),
  2. `figma.component_set_node_id` from spec,
  3. name-based lookup (allowed only when deterministic ID is unavailable).

### `qa`

- Minimum 2 items: property match check + token validity check.
- Additional items for component-specific invariants.

## File naming

- One file per component: `<snake_case>.yml` (e.g., `status_bar.yml`).
- File naming and `name` normalization must follow `component-name-normalization.mdc`.

## Template

`docs/_spec/components/_template.yml` is the canonical structural template - copy it for every new component.

- Every required top-level field is present; use `TBD` for unknown values (never omit fields).
- `properties` defaults to `[]` so a newly copied draft spec stays valid; uncomment the type-group examples and replace placeholders with concrete values.
- Do NOT create a new spec by writing fields from memory; always start from the template to prevent omissions.
- The template is the structural authority; this rule is the semantic authority.
